  "doc.desc": "Clicking a button and calling setCount(c => c + 1) does not edit a single DOM node right away. Following the React 19.3.1 source, this essay unpacks that line: immutable JSX element objects, the Fiber linked list and double buffering, two-pass O(n) list diffing and keys, hooks as a call-ordered linked list, subtreeFlags bubbling, the three commit phases and effect timing, root event delegation and microtask batching, 31-bit Lane scheduling, and the November 2026 frontier across React Compiler, Server Components, Activity, and View Transitions. Nine hands-on models implement the same algorithms and check them against React 19.3.1 itself.",
