  "ch5.say.normal": "Cursors stepped cleanly 0→1→2. Breaking the circular ring at <code>tail.next</code> replayed updates from {prev} to produce <em>{next}</em> with an empty <code>baseQueue</code>.",
  "ch5.say.skipped": "Update #1 (TransitionLane) was skipped for low priority, so it and every update after it copied into <em>baseQueue</em> ({base} saved) while <code>baseState</code> stayed at {bstate} to prevent state drift.",
  "ch5.say.error": "Cursor mismatch! Skipping Hook 0 shifted <code>useState('Ada')</code> onto slot 0 (reading <em>{next}</em>) and threw off the remaining count—triggering React's hook-order error.",
  "ch5.p4": "With the default `+1 then ×2` queue starting from 10, `(10 + 1) × 2` lands on <strong>22</strong>. Flip the order to `×2 then +1`, and replaying the same two updaters yields `21`—which is why functional updaters always receive the previous updater's output rather than a stale render snapshot.",
  "ch5.limit": "The model omits: `useState`'s eager-state fast path (bailing out before scheduling when `Object.is(eagerState, currentState)`), React dev-mode double invocation of components/reducers, and `fiber.updateQueue` storing passive/layout effect rings separately.",
  "ch6.title": "beginWork, completeWork, and subtreeFlags",
  "toc.ch6": "beginWork, completeWork, and subtreeFlags",
  "ch6.law": "When one leaf changes inside ten thousand components, walking the entire tree again during commit would waste most of your frame budget. React bubbles dirty bits upward with bitwise OR inside `completeWork` so commit touches only flagged branches.",
  "ch6.p1": "Every node visited during render passes through two steps: `beginWork` on the way down—calling component functions and diffing children, or bailing out early (`attemptEarlyBailoutIfNoScheduledUpdate`) when props and lanes are clean—followed by `completeWork` on the way back up.",
  "ch6.p2": "For host tags like `&lt;div&gt;`, `completeWork` allocates new DOM elements (`createInstance`) and appends child DOM nodes (`appendAllChildren`) off-screen on mount, or computes prop diffs on updates. Then `bubbleProperties` runs on every completed Fiber, bitwise-ORing each child's `flags | subtreeFlags` into the parent's `subtreeFlags` (and `lanes | childLanes` into `childLanes`).",
  "dg.flags.cap": "Figure 6. completeWork bubbles flags upward via bitwise OR into subtreeFlags. Any branch whose subtreeFlags bitmask is 0 gets skipped outright during commit.",
  "dg.flags.aria": "Diagram: left branch leaf carries flag 0x04 bubbling up to Main and Root subtreeFlags, while clean right branch Nav has subtreeFlags 0x00 and is skipped",
  "dg.flags.root": "Root sub:0x04",
  "dg.flags.left": "Main sub:0x04",
  "dg.flags.clean": "Nav sub:0x00",
