  "dg.flags.skip": "Mask 0: skip branch",
  "ch6.p3": "Once commit starts from the root, it checks `(child.subtreeFlags & CommitMask) !== 0` before descending. Clean subtrees are never even entered. In our 15-node tree, updating one deep leaf (`Post2`) sets `Update` (`0x0004`), lets render bail out of untouched siblings, and leaves commit visiting only 5 ancestor nodes while skipping <strong>10</strong> clean nodes (<strong>67%</strong> skipped).",
  "ch6.model.title": "Traversal and subtreeFlags skip counter",
  "ch6.model.how": "Pick an update preset or click any node directly on the canvas to mark it dirty. Watch flags bubble up to the root in hex and compare Render visits against Commit skips.",
  "ch6.ctl.preset": "Dirty scenario",
  "ch6.pre.leaf": "One deep leaf update",
  "ch6.pre.two": "Two leaves (Update + Placement)",
  "ch6.pre.del": "Nav ChildDeletion",
  "ch6.pre.shell": "Multi-branch Shell update",
  "ch6.cv.aria": "15-node component tree highlighting Render visits, bubbled hex subtreeFlags, and clean branches skipped in Commit",
  "ch6.cv.legVis": "Render visited",
  "ch6.cv.legCom": "Commit entered",
  "ch6.cv.legSkip": "Clean skipped",
  "ch6.read.render": "Render visited",
  "ch6.read.commit": "Commit entered",
  "ch6.read.skip": "Commit skipped",
  "ch6.read.mask": "Root subtreeFlags",
  "ch6.say": "Root collected <code>subtreeFlags = {mask}</code>. Out of {total} nodes, Render visited {render} (bailing out of clean subtrees), and synchronous Commit entered just <em>{commit}</em> nodes while skipping <em>{skip}</em> clean nodes ({pct} skipped).",
  "ch6.p4": "Compare a single leaf update against a high-level `Shell` update: the clean `Nav`, `Sidebar`, and `Footer` subtrees remain completely untouched during commit. React 19 also preserves static flags across renders using `StaticMask` (`0x47f00000`, or `1206910976`) instead of wiping them on every alternate reuse.",
  "ch6.limit": "The model omits: Suspense error unwinding via `unwindUnitOfWork`, context dependency propagation (`didReceiveUpdate`), and the exact bit differences across `MutationMask` (`13878`), `LayoutMask` (`8772`), and `PassiveMask` (`10256`).",
  "ch7.title": "Commit phases and when Effects run",
  "toc.ch7": "Commit phases and when Effects run",
  "ch7.law": "Render can pause whenever time runs out, but commit cannot pause for a millisecond—showing half-inserted nodes would break layout on screen. React runs three synchronous commit sub-phases, lets the browser paint, and schedules `useEffect` into a separate task afterward.",
  "ch7.p1": "In `commitRootImpl` (React 19.3.1), once `workInProgress` finishes, React executes a strict sequence on the main thread:",
  "ch7.s1": "<strong>BeforeMutation</strong>: Reads pre-mutation DOM metrics (for class `getSnapshotBeforeUpdate`) while `current` is still live.",
  "ch7.s2": "<strong>Mutation</strong>: Walks subtrees matching `MutationMask` to append, insert, remove, and update DOM nodes, and runs `useInsertionEffect` plus previous `useLayoutEffect` cleanups.",
  "ch7.s3": "<strong>The pointer flip (`root.current = finishedWork`)</strong>: One assignment swaps the live tree reference to the newly committed Fibers.",
  "ch7.s4": "<strong>Layout (still before paint!)</strong>: Walks `LayoutMask` to attach `ref`s and run <strong>`useLayoutEffect`</strong> synchronously. The DOM is already updated, yet <strong>no pixels have been painted yet</strong>—measuring `getBoundingClientRect()` and calling `setState` inside `useLayoutEffect` triggers a synchronous re-render and DOM update before the frame hits the glass, preventing visual flicker at the price of delaying paint.",
  "ch7.s5": "<strong>Browser Layout & Paint</strong>: React yields the main thread; the browser lays out CSS, rasterizes, and sends the frame toward the 16.67 ms refresh budget (<a href=\"../../systems/how-pixels-reach-a-screen/#ch3\">How Pixels Reach a Screen, chapter 3</a>).",
  "ch7.s6": "<strong>Passive (`flushPassiveEffects`)</strong>: Scheduled earlier via Scheduler `NormalPriority` (`MessageChannel`), running `useEffect` cleanups and callbacks <em>after</em> the browser has painted.",
  "dg.commit.cap": "Figure 7. Main-thread timeline from Render through useEffect. Gold and red commit phases block Browser Paint directly; violet useEffect runs in a later task without delaying the first frame.",
  "dg.commit.aria": "Diagram: main-thread order of Render, Mutation, LayoutEffect (useLayoutEffect), Browser Paint, and asynchronous PassiveEffect (useEffect)",
