  "ch7.hk.passive": "useEffect (post-paint)",
  "ch7.cv.aria": "Main-thread horizontal timeline showing Render, Commit phases, the 16.67 ms frame deadline, Browser Paint, and Passive Effects",
  "ch7.cv.x": "Main-thread time (ms)",
  "ch7.cv.budget": "16.67 ms budget",
  "ch7.cv.paintAt": "Painted at",
  "ch7.read.paint": "Time to first paint",
  "ch7.read.total": "Total incl. Effects",
  "ch7.read.drop": "Dropped 60 Hz frames",
  "ch7.read.flash": "First-frame flicker",
  "ch7.val.yes": "1-frame flash",
  "ch7.val.no": "No flicker",
  "ch7.say.layoutOk": "<code>useLayoutEffect</code> measured and repositioned the tooltip synchronously before paint (first paint at <em>{paint} ms</em>), beating the {budget} ms frame deadline with <em>zero flicker</em>.",
  "ch7.say.layoutSlow": "Using <code>useLayoutEffect</code> prevented position flicker, but blocking the main thread pushed first paint out to <em>{paint} ms</em>—dropping <em>{drop} frame(s)</em> on a 60 Hz display.",
  "ch7.say.passiveFlash": "First paint finished cleanly at <em>{paint} ms</em> without blocking, but because <code>useEffect</code> measured dimensions and called <code>setState</code> after paint, users see the tooltip <em>flash for 1 frame</em> at the wrong spot first.",
  "ch7.p2": "With default 4 ms Render, 1.5 ms Mutation, and 6 ms `useLayoutEffect`, synchronous pre-paint re-measurement hits the glass in <strong>15.6 ms</strong> inside one frame; moving that adjustment into `useEffect` paints earlier at <strong>13.8 ms</strong> but flashes one wrong frame first. The trade-off is simple: keep side effects in `useEffect` unless avoiding a visible one-frame layout jump requires `useLayoutEffect`.",
  "ch7.limit": "The model omits: variable browser style/layout cost on complex CSS (modeled as a fixed 2.0 ms paint parameter), `useInsertionEffect` style injection during Mutation, and `flushSync` forcing pending passive effects to flush early.",
  "ch8.title": "Event delegation and automatic batching",
  "toc.ch8": "Event delegation and automatic batching",
  "ch8.law": "Even with ten thousand `&lt;button onClick={...}&gt;` elements on a page, React never calls `addEventListener` ten thousand times. It attaches one listener per event type on the root container, maps the target DOM node back to its Fiber, walks `return` pointers to simulate capture and bubble, and batches every `setState` in that turn inside one microtask.",
  "ch8.p1": "When `createRoot(container)` mounts, `listenToAllSupportedEvents(container)` attaches <strong>1</strong> delegated root listener pair per supported event type (capture and bubble). Meanwhile, React tags every managed DOM node with a hidden property `__reactFiber$&lt;random&gt;` pointing straight to its host Fiber.",
  "ch8.p2": "When you click a nested `&lt;button&gt;`, the native browser event bubbles up to the root container. React's `dispatchEvent` grabs `nativeEvent.target`, resolves the button's Fiber in O(1), and walks `fiber.return` upward to the root—collecting every `onClickCapture` (replayed top-down) and `onClick` (replayed bottom-up). Calling `e.stopPropagation()` inside a React `onClick` halts React's synthetic walk along `return` pointers, though remember the native event already bubbled to `#root` before React ran.",
  "ch8.p3": "Just as important is what happens when your handler updates multiple states in a row. Inside React 19's `ensureRootIsScheduled`, whether `setState` runs inside a React `onClick`, a `setTimeout`, or a `Promise.then`, every update enters a queue and schedules one microtask (`processRootScheduleInMicrotask`). Once synchronous code finishes, <strong>3</strong> consecutive `setState` calls coalesce into <strong>1</strong> render and commit—unless you wrap each update in `ReactDOM.flushSync`, forcing <strong>3</strong> immediate synchronous commits.",
  "dg.events.cap": "Figure 8. A click bubbles natively to #root's single delegated listener. React locates the button Fiber via __reactFiber$, walks return pointers for capture (cyan) and bubble (violet), and batches updates at the microtask checkpoint.",
  "dg.events.aria": "Diagram: native event bubbling from button to div#root, synthetic capture and bubble along Fiber return pointers, and microtask batching",
  "dg.events.root": "div#root (1 native listener)",
  "dg.events.card": "section.card",
